                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %strong thick
            (in the strong sense) if for every exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                  %mo ″
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \longrightarrow M\longrightarrow M''\longrightarrow M'\longrightarrow 0
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ″
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M''
            is in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'
            are in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            In words, it is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            closed under subobjects, quotients and extensions (e.g.
            %a{:href => "#Dichev09"} Dichev 2009
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"} Pierre Gabriel
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Des+Cat%C3%A9gories+Ab%C3%A9liennes"} Des Catégories Abéliennes
          %p
            In any abelian category all subobjects are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"} cokernels
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
          %p
            Another way to pack the same definition is that thick subcategory of an abelian category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologizing+subcategory"} topologizing subcategory
            closed under extensions.
          %h4#remarks_on_terminology_in_abelian_context Remarks on terminology in abelian context
          %p
            For some authors the thick subcategory is also called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+subcategory"} Serre subcategory
            (in a weak sense), the term which we reserve for (generally) a stronger notion.
          %p
            For any subcategory of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            one denotes by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{T}
            the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            generated by all objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            for which any (nonzero)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotient"} subquotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            has a (nonzero)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\subset \bar{T}
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologizing+subcategory"} topologizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{T}
            is always thick in the stronger sense.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+subcategory"} Serre subcategories
            in the strong sense are those (nonempty) subcategories which are stable under the operation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mapsto\bar{T}
          %h2#serre_quotient_category Serre quotient category
          %p
            Following the extensions of an early work of Serre by Grothendieck and Gabriel, for any thick subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/T
            as the one having the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi colim
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A/T)(X,Y) := colim A(X',Y/Y')
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            runs through all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'\subset X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y'\subset Y
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/X' \in Ob T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y'\in Ob T
          %p It remains to define bilinear composition laws:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{A/T}(M, N)\times Hom_{A/T}(N, P)\longrightarrow Hom_{A/T}(M,P).
          %blockquote
            %p
              For this, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}
              be an element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{A/T}(M, N)
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{g}
              be an element of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo ,
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{A/T}(N, P)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}
              is the image of a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: M'\to N/N'
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/M'
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N'
              are objects of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{g}
              is the image of a morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi N
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi P
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:N'\to P/P'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N/N'
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P'
              are objects of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M''
              designates the inverse image
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo ″
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi N
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi N
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}((N''+N')/N')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/M''
              belongs to
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              the morphism from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M''
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N''+N')/N'
              which is induced by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(N''\cap N')
              is an object of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P''
              denotes the sum
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi N
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P'+g(N''\cap N')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P''
              belongs to
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
              the morphism of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N''/(N''\cap N')
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi P
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P/P''
              which is induced by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              be the composition of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N''+ N')/N'
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N''/(N''\cap N')
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi can
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo ′
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi P
                    %mo ″
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M'' \overset{f^'}\longrightarrow (N''+N')/N' \overset{can}\longrightarrow N''/(N''\cap N')\overset{g^'}\longrightarrow P/P''.
            %p
              The image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi h
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{h}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{A/T}(M, P)
              depends only on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{g}
              and not on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/T
              by equality
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∘
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi h
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{g}\circ\overline{f} = \overline{h}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/T
              a category.
          %p
            (adapted from Gabriel,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Des+Cat%C3%A9gories+Ab%C3%A9liennes"} Des Catégories Abéliennes
          %p
            The quotient functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \colon A\to A/T
            is obvious.
          %p
            Notice that the set of morphisms is indeed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            by the Gabriel-Zisman localizing at the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            of all morphisms whose kernel and cokernel are in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            admits the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
          %p
            A basic example is the quotient of the category of abelian groups modulo the torsion groups. This category is equivalent to the category of
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            to the scalar extension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{Q}
            %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0J"} Stacks Project, Tag 0B0J
            for a proof.)
          %h3#localizing_subcategories Localizing subcategories
          %p
            A thick subcategory (here always in the strong sense) is said to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizing+subcategory"} localizing
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is thick and the Serre quotient functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            admits a right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/T\to A
            = succeed "." do
              %strong section functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/T
            is then a reflective subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            admits a section functor, and the converse holds if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has injective envelopes. A thick subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\subset A
            is a coreflective iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,F)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+theory"} torsion theory
            where
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ob
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \coloneqq \{X\in Ob A\,|\,A(T,X) = 0\}
          %h2#thick_subcategories_and_saturation Thick subcategories and saturation
          %p
            Recall that a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            of morphisms with category of fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_\Sigma
            is called
            %em saturated
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            coincides with the class of morphisms inverted by the canonical functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}\to \mathcal{C}_\Sigma
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an abelian category,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a thick subcategory in the strong sense and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_T
            be the class of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that their kernel and cokernel are in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_T
            has a right and a left calculus of fractions and is saturated for the canonical functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A\to A/T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            maps to zero objects precisely the objects in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Conversely, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a saturated class of morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with a calculus of fractions on the right and on the left. Then the full subcategory on the objects that are mapped to zero by the canonical
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A\to A_\Sigma
            is thick. In other words, there is a bijection between thick subcategories in the strong sense and saturated classes of morphisms with a calculus of fractions on the right and on the left.
          %p
            (For this material see Gabriel and Zisman,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"} Calculus of fractions and homotopy theory
            I.2.5.d) and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schubert70b"} Schubert 1970
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thick+subcategory+theorem"} thick subcategory theorem
          %h2#references References
          %h3#abelian_context Abelian context
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Des catégories abéliennes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=BSMF_1962__90__323_0"} numdam
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Localization_in_categories"} Localization of categories
                (for Serre quotient category)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+L.+Rosenberg"}> A. L. Rosenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative algebraic geometry and representations of quantized algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 330
          %p It is called “dense subcategory” (see page 165) in Popescu:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                N. Popescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abelian+categories+with+applications+to+rings+and+modules"} Abelian categories with applications to rings and modules
            %li#Schubert70b
              %p
                H. Schubert,
                %em Kategorien II
                , Springer Heidelberg 1970.
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
          %ul
            %li#Dichev09
              Nikolay Dimitrov Dichev,
              %em Thick subcategories for quiver representations
              2009 (
              %a{:href => "https://d-nb.info/995877602/34"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#triangulated_context Triangulated context
          %ul
            %li#Murayama
              %p
                Takumi Murayama,
                %em The classification of thick subcategories and Balmer’s reconstruction theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.purdue.edu/~murayama/NeemanBalmer.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em Thick subcategories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture26.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#StacksProject05RA
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05RA"} Quotients of triangulated categories
